ithm Fundamentals#4. Log Rules Derived from Intuition#4.5 $\\log(a+b)$ has no nice form *(at [[37:43]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2263s))*#{1}":[182,192],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#4. Log Rules Derived from Intuition#4.6 Why $\\log_0$ doesn't exist *(at [[44:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2654s))*":[193,200],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#4. Log Rules Derived from Intuition#4.6 Why $\\log_0$ doesn't exist *(at [[44:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2654s))*#{1}":[195,200],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#5. Real-World Logarithmic Scales":[201,226],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#5. Real-World Logarithmic Scales#5.1 The Richter scale: every +1 means ×32 *(at [[46:05]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2765s))*":[203,219],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#5. Real-World Logarithmic Scales#5.1 The Richter scale: every +1 means ×32 *(at [[46:05]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2765s))*#{1}":[205,219],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#5. Real-World Logarithmic Scales#5.2 Halfway is multiplicative *(at [[39:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2391s))*":[220,226],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#5. Real-World Logarithmic Scales#5.2 Halfway is multiplicative *(at [[39:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=2391s))*#{1}":[222,226],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#6. Translating Between Bases":[227,289],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#6. Translating Between Bases#6.1 The 0.3 magic: $\\log_{10}(2) \\approx 0.3$ *(at [[56:40]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=3400s))*":[229,249],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#6. Translating Between Bases#6.1 The 0.3 magic: $\\log_{10}(2) \\approx 0.3$ *(at [[56:40]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=3400s))*#{1}":[231,249],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#6. Translating Between Bases#6.2 The change-of-base formula *(at [[72:22]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cEvgcoyZvB4&t=4342s))*":[250,262],"#Logarithm Fundamentals#6. Translating Between Bases#6.2 The change-of-base formula *(at [[72:22